{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Get you up from among</b> etc. Meaning: He is not speaking to Moses and Aaron, but to those who were not included among the complainers. And the trustworthy witness said it: <b>and He spoke</b> etc. <b>saying</b> — and the meaning is to others. And the verse was precise in saying <b>this</b>, to point with a finger at the complainers, to exclude all others who are not included in the decree of destruction. And by this is resolved why it was necessary to say <b>Get you up</b> — for surely HaShem is able to slay a wicked person before a righteous person, as in the slaying of the firstborn of Egypt. But according to our words, that He is speaking about the rest of the people who were not included among the complainers, because they were included in the decree of the spies, there is need for the matter to distance themselves so that the attribute of justice not strike them. And the statement <b>in a moment</b> I have explained (Numbers 16:21)."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:36.016995489Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}